            <ArticleTitle>Synthesis of some N-substituted 3,4-pyrroledicarboximides as potential CNS depressive agents.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>9-16</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>As a continuation of our work on N-[4-aryl(heteroaryl)piperazin-1-ylalkyl]-3,4-pyrro ledicarboximides, which were characterized by strong analgesic activity and CNS depressive action, several novel N-substituted 3,4-pyrroledicarboximides were prepared and eleven representatives were examined in a series of in vivo CNS tests. A few of these compounds displayed a similar profile of biological selectivity to that of 3,4-pyrroledicarboximides described previously; their structure-activity relationships are discussed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
